[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mFor a new project, tooling is cheapest to set up before any code exists. Which do you want from the start?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Linting + auto-format
  [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier with aggressive defaults. Catches mistakes and ends formatting debates. Low cost even on a vanilla [39m
  [38;5;246mproject.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit test infrastructure
  [38;5;246mA test runner, a layout, and one passing fixture. The storage seam and reminder logic are the parts genuinely worth [39m
  [38;5;246mtesting.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright driving a real browser. Highest value for a UI app, highest setup and maintenance cost.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None for now
  [38;5;246mSkip all tooling; just the app. Fastest start, and retrofitting tests later is harder than adding them now.[39m
